# Claude Code worktrees: isolated checkouts, never part of the tree
.claude/worktrees/

# Credentials. Carried into worktrees by .worktreeinclude, never committed.
.env
.env.local

# Personal, per-machine permission approvals. Project rules live in
# .claude/settings.json and ARE committed.
.claude/settings.local.json

# miniflare's own cache directory. It is created wherever a suite that drives
# the REAL plane is run from — bio-plane/ has always had one, and UI-13's
# intent-write harness makes one under civicos-ui/ too. Never part of the tree.
.wrangler/

# NEGATIVE-CONTROL PENS. A control driver copies pristine sources into a pen
# inside its own worktree (WORKER.md: never a shared scratchpad) and restores
# from them; UI-50's `.ui50-harness/` and UI-42's `.ui42-harness/` are the
# pattern. The drivers remove their pen on a clean run, but a driver INTERRUPTED
# mid-arm leaves one behind — and an untracked scratch file left in a worktree
# has already been swept into another item's walk (CLAIMS.md, UI-38's delegation
# to M0 about `bio-plane/test/op-claims.test.mjs`). Ignored so an interrupted
# control cannot become somebody else's corpus.
.ui*-harness/
# PL-13's pen, same rule and named for its item rather than squeezed into the
# `.ui*` pattern: a plane-side control driver needs a pen too, and naming it
# `.ui…` so an existing line would cover it is the kind of small dishonesty that
# makes the next reader mistrust the whole file.
.pl13-harness/
# D-251's pen, same rule and named for its item for the same reason: an
# interrupted control run must not leave a copy of `pdfstructure.mjs` sitting
# untracked where the next walk can enrol it as a source file.
.d251-control-pristine/
# D-271's pen. Named for the item rather than the area because the item is a
# plane item; the `.ui*` spelling above is an accident of which area needed a
# pen first, not a rule about who may have one.
.d271-harness/
# D-266's pen, and its BASELINE CAPTURES too. Same rule, same reason for its own
# line rather than a widened `.pl*` glob. This item's driver arms `store.mjs` and
# restores from here, and the same directory holds the three instrument outputs
# the item quotes as its baseline — kept inside the worktree so no other session's
# battery can overwrite the figures this one reports.
.d266-harness/
# D-267's pen, named for its item for the same reason PL-13's is.
.d267-harness/
# D-280's pen, named for its item for the same reason D-267's and PL-13's are.
# An interrupted driver must not leave an untracked file that becomes somebody
# else's corpus (M0-15: `git stash -u` is repository-wide, not per-worktree).
.d280-harness/
